      "rationale": "📖️ The case's oracle role (`../🦀️.rs`): `djpeg -v -v` traces every marker libjpeg-turbo parses — the SOFn code, each frame component's sampling factors, every DHT table's class and id and a DAC segment — and `rdjpgcom -verbose` reports the sample precision. Each kind is applied to those axes as ITU-T T.81 defines the field and the class is read off the specification's own tables; this repository's decoder, snapshot and checker are never consulted. This replaces the Pillow reader registered for this capability, which no case ran and which cannot see the DHT or DAC axes (Pillow's JPEG plugin skips both markers). Installed on macOS through Homebrew (`jpeg-turbo`) and in the devcontainer through `libjpeg-turbo-progs`; where the commands are missing the oracle phase records the case as oracle-unavailable."
